cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SalmonTElocus, please cite it using the metadata below, and also
  cite SalmonTE and Salmon (see references).
title: "SalmonTElocus: per-locus transposable element quantification with Salmon"
abstract: >-
  SalmonTElocus quantifies transposable elements (TEs) from RNA-seq at the
  level of individual genomic copies. It is a rewrite of SalmonTE that indexes
  every TE copy cut from the genome, reports per-locus and per-subfamily
  counts with genomic coordinates, optionally labels copies by gene context
  (exon/intron/intergenic) without counting genes, and runs DESeq2 with
  TE- or gene-based size factors.
type: software
